Additional Terms: Liquidated Damages for Unauthorised Commercial Use

The following terms supplement the Business Source License above and apply
specifically to any Commercial Use of the Licensed Work that violates the
Additional Use Grant.

1.  Nature of Damages

    The Licensor has invested substantial original time, research, and
    intellectual effort in developing the Licensed Work — including its
    classification heuristics, adapter protocols, catalog design, and the
    harness-engineering methodology it embodies. Unauthorised Commercial Use
    causes harm that is difficult to quantify precisely. The parties therefore
    agree that the amounts below constitute a reasonable pre-estimate of
    damages and not a penalty.

2.  Liquidated Damages — Tiered by Organisation Size

    Any person or legal entity that makes Commercial Use of the Licensed Work
    without a valid commercial licence shall owe the Licensor, upon demand,
    the GREATER of (a) or (b) below, per production instance or deployment
    unit, per calendar month of unauthorised use, retroactive to the first
    date on which Commercial Use commenced:

    (a) Tier-based monthly amount:

        Tier 1 — Individual / Micro
                 (sole trader; or fewer than 5 employees; or gross annual
                 revenue below USD 250,000 / BRL 1,375,000):
                 USD 10,000 / BRL 55,000 per instance per month.

        Tier 2 — Startup
                 (5–50 employees; or annual revenue USD 250k–5M /
                 BRL 1.375M–27.5M):
                 USD 50,000 / BRL 275,000 per instance per month.

        Tier 3 — Growth
                 (51–500 employees; or annual revenue USD 5M–100M /
                 BRL 27.5M–550M):
                 USD 150,000 / BRL 825,000 per instance per month.

        Tier 4 — Enterprise
                 (more than 500 employees; or annual revenue above
                 USD 100,000,000 / BRL 550,000,000):
                 USD 500,000 / BRL 2,750,000 per instance per month.

    (b) Revenue-based monthly amount:

        20% (twenty percent) of the infringing party's gross monthly revenue
        directly or indirectly attributable to the product, service, workflow,
        or system that incorporates or is enabled by the Licensed Work, for
        each month of unauthorised use.

    Where both USD and BRL amounts are asserted in the same proceeding, the
    Licensor shall recover the denomination yielding the higher amount at the
    prevailing exchange rate on the date of demand, not both simultaneously.

3.  Minimum Per-Action Damages

    In addition to the recurring amounts in section 2, the infringing party
    shall pay:

    (a) A minimum lump sum of USD 250,000 / BRL 1,375,000 per enforcement
        action, regardless of duration, as compensation for investigation,
        legal preparation, reputational harm, and lost licensing opportunity.

    (b) All reasonable legal fees and costs on a full-indemnity basis.

    (c) Full disgorgement of all profits derived from the unauthorised use.

4.  Wilful Infringement Multiplier

    If the Licensor demonstrates that the infringing party had actual
    knowledge of this Licence and proceeded with Commercial Use regardless,
    all amounts in sections 2 and 3 shall be multiplied by five (5×).

5.  Jurisdiction and Governing Law

    The Licensor may bring an action in any of the following forums,
    at sole election:

    (a) Foro Central da Comarca de São Paulo, Estado de São Paulo, Brazil,
        governed by Brazilian law (Lei 9.610/98, Lei 9.609/98, and the
        Brazilian Civil Code).

    (b) Any court of competent jurisdiction in the country or US state where
        the infringing party is incorporated, domiciled, or operates its
        principal place of business.

    (c) The Southern District of New York, USA, governed by New York law
        and the US Copyright Act (17 U.S.C. § 101 et seq.).

    The infringing party consents to personal jurisdiction in each forum
    above and waives any objection on grounds of inconvenient forum.

6.  Good Faith Cure (One-Time)

    If an infringing party (i) permanently ceases all Commercial Use within
    15 days of receiving written notice from the Licensor, and (ii) pays all
    accrued damages under section 2 within 45 days of such notice, the
    Licensor may — at sole and unreviewable discretion — waive the minimum
    lump sum in 3(a) and the wilful multiplier in section 4.

    This cure provision:
    — may be exercised at most once per legal entity;
    — does not apply if Commercial Use continued after a prior written notice;
    — does not constitute a licence or an admission that the cure payment is
      adequate compensation.

7.  Intellectual Property

    All copyright, trade secret, and other intellectual property rights in
    the Licensed Work are owned exclusively by Tiago de Carvalho Vilas Boas.
    Publication of source code does not constitute a dedication to the public
    domain or a waiver of any right. The Author reserves the right to pursue
    copyright infringement claims independently of any contractual claim
    under this Licence.

8.  Contributor Assignment

    By submitting a contribution to the official repository, the contributor
    irrevocably assigns to Tiago de Carvalho Vilas Boas all copyright in
    that contribution and grants the Licensor the right to use, modify, and
    relicence it under any terms, including proprietary terms. The Licensor
    will credit significant contributors in project documentation.

9.  Severability

    If any provision of these Additional Terms is held invalid or
    unenforceable, that provision shall be enforced to the maximum extent
    permissible and all remaining provisions continue in full force.

